          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>Which of the following is NOT one of the four anatomical components of congenita</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>Which of the following is NOT one of the four anatomical components of congenital talipes equinovarus (clubfoot)?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Hindfoot equinus</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Equinus (plantarflexion at the ankle, resembling a horse's hoof) IS one of the four CTEV components.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Forefoot adductus</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Forefoot adductus (medial deviation of the forefoot) IS one of the four CTEV components.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Hindfoot valgus</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. The hindfoot deformity in CTEV is varus (inversion), not valgus (eversion). The four components are Cavus, Adductus, Varus, and Equinus — remembered by the mnemonic CAVE.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Midfoot cavus</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Cavus (high medial longitudinal arch) IS one of the four CTEV components.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The four components are hindfoot equinus, hindfoot varus, forefoot adductus, and midfoot cavus. Valgus means eversion — the OPPOSITE of varus (inversion). Remembering the mnemonic CAVE helps: Cavus, Adductus, Varus, Equinus."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Well done. The four components of CTEV are Cavus, Adductus, Varus, and Equinus (CAVE). Valgus (eversion) is the opposite deformity to varus and is not a feature of clubfoot."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
